From: Teguh Sobirin <teguh@sobir.in>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: add WCN7750 on the WPSS hybrid bus

The Retroid Pocket Duo's Wi-Fi, a WCN7750 whose WLAN Q6 runs on the
Eliza WPSS: MSI as a block of GIC SPIs, the register BAR reported over
QMI and reached through the PCI parts' static windows, and the
companion RF die's rails, interconnect path and WLAN_EN sequenced from
an rproc subdev. Mostly Teguh Sobirin's RetroidPocket/linux series, as
backported to 7.2 by armada (armada-os/armada b91b786), squashed in
order:

  1140 move MSI state from ath12k_pci to ath12k_base
  1141 share the register window geometry with the core
  1142 let the MSI CE/DP IRQ setup serve platform devices
  1143 allow receive-only services in map_service_to_pipe
  1144 keep the CE interrupt mask balanced across restarts
  1145 add an optional cfg_static_window hif op
  1146 take the shadow register base from hw_params
  1147 support targets with fixed firmware memory
  1148 cap the shadow register configuration at 38 entries
  1149 add the QMI device info request
  1150 send ddr_range and gpio_info in host_cap
  1151 support cold boot calibration
  1152 track the firmware generation across recovery
  1153 add ath12k_core_firmware_crashed()
  1154 stop touching srngs after the HAL is torn down
  1155 tolerate a missing hwmon device on thermal cleanup
  1156 guard the link peer table against concurrent teardown
  1157 add the WCN7750 copy engine configuration
  1158 add WCN7750 hw1.0
  1159 ahb: add the WCN7750 hybrid-bus transport
  1160 unwind WCN7750 probe failures
  1161 dt-bindings: describe WCN7750 resources
  1183 associate WCN7750 as HE on 6 GHz

Rebased onto 7.3.5 with our `1002`-`1032`:
- 1140: 7.3 keeps ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_POWERED_UP (`1031`) after the flag it
  drops.
- 1150: 7.3's host_cap already carries dynamic_mem_support (TLV 0x33).
  gpio_info (0x2D) goes before it and the max length becomes 407
  (7.3's 265 + the 142 armada added).
- 1151: the calibration mode is ATH12K_QMI_FIRMWARE_MODE_CALIBRATION in
  7.3's ath12k_qmi_firmware_mode enum, not a bare define.
- 1159: 7.3 picks the AHB hif ops and UserPD from a per-SoC
  ath12k_ahb_desc and has its own UserPD rproc_info. WCN7750 gets a desc
  with ath12k_ahb_hif_ops_wcn7750, sets hybrid_bus and the wifi7 PCI
  register base in the wifi7 probe, and skips the UserPD id; the
  hybrid branch in ath12k_ahb_probe() replaces configure_rproc +
  config_rproc_irq + config_irq, and the error/remove paths unwind it
  (the IPQ path keeps 7.3's rproc_info locking).
Not built here; not run on a Duo.
